**How to implement.** In OpticalConstructor.Domain, beside MaterialLibrary, declare the mutating materials write-seam: DispersionFilter = AnyDispersion | OnlyDispersive | OnlyNonDispersive; MaterialQuery (text : string, category : MaterialCategory option, dispersion : DispersionFilter - MaterialCategory at MaterialLibrary.fs:21); extend MaterialError with DuplicateMaterialId, MaterialStillReferenced and InvalidMaterial, each carrying reason : string; and the [<ReferenceEquality>] record MaterialProxy with listMaterials : unit -> Result<MaterialEntry list, MaterialError>, searchMaterials : MaterialQuery -> Result<MaterialEntry list, MaterialError>, tryGetMaterial : MaterialId -> Result<MaterialEntry option, MaterialError>, addMaterial : MaterialEntry -> Result<unit, MaterialError>, updateMaterial : MaterialEntry -> Result<unit, MaterialError>, removeMaterial : MaterialId -> Result<unit, MaterialError>, following the LibraryProxy functional-proxy convention (ElementId.fs:178-184). Provide a mock (an inline stub record over a fixed entry list) plus a mock-driven test in OpticalConstructor.Tests exercising every field.

**Acceptance.** After the step, a mock-driven test MUST build a stub MaterialProxy and exercise all six functions through their exact signatures, and it passes.
